[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2507420827","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99815#issuecomment-2507420827","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99815","id":2507420827,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VdDSb","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-29T09:34:04Z","updated_at":"2024-11-29T10:18:50Z","body":"Idk about operators, but at least functions with -O2 optimization level will be inlined by compiler if it is needed even without inline attribute. At least as far as I remember. So this one will make difference only for Godot Web builds which use -Os.\r\nBut it would probably be better if this is confirmed or refuted by someone more knowledgeable in C++ (as I'm mostly C programmer for embedded systems).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2507420827/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2507480443","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99815#issuecomment-2507480443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99815","id":2507480443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VdR17","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-29T10:06:56Z","updated_at":"2024-11-29T10:18:38Z","body":"> Idk about operators, but at least functions with -O2 optimization level will be inlined by compiler if it is needed even without inline attribute. At least as far as I remember. So this one will make difference only for Godot Web builds which use -Os. But it would probably be better if this is confirmed or refuted by someone more knowledgeable in C++ (as I'm mostly C programmer for embedded embedded systems).\r\n\r\nThis is not the case if the function is defined inside a module. In this case the function is considered to be blackbox, and a call is unavoidable. It may still be inlined by the LTO later, although not all release builds of Godot have LTO enabled. Plus, when it's LTO's turn, a lot of optimizations are already over.\r\nThe only option that makes this change redundant is single compilation unit (scu), which i don't know if it's enabled for official release builds (Edit: looks like it's only enabled in parts of the linux pipeline). But in any case, it can't hurt to move `==` next to `!=` to have consistency.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2507480443/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2509202661","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99815#issuecomment-2509202661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99815","id":2509202661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Vj2Tl","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-30T20:22:26Z","updated_at":"2024-11-30T20:22:26Z","body":"The change makes sense, I don't see a reason why `!=` would be defined somewhere else than `==`. I'd ask @reduz if there is a technical reason for that.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2509202661/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2511767951","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99815#issuecomment-2511767951","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99815","id":2511767951,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VtomP","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-02T14:57:51Z","updated_at":"2024-12-02T14:57:51Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2511767951/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]